WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.360
Begin with the selected pollen section.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.960
A marks the outer exine and B the inner intine.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:10.640
C points to a germ pore region where the exine is interrupted.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:15.840
The resistant exine contains sporopollenin, while intine is mainly cellulose

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:16.400
and pectin.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:20.940
The opening in exine is not an empty hole through every layer of the living

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:21.460
pollen grain.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:25.380
During germination, the developing tube emerges through an aperture.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.280
Only one germ pore region is selected here; pollen grains vary in aperture

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.220
number, shape and surface pattern.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.320
This smooth teaching outline is therefore not a species diagnosis or a

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.020
measurement of wall thickness.

00:00:38.616 --> 00:00:42.456
D labels the vegetative nucleus within the large vegetative cell.

00:00:43.596 --> 00:00:47.956
E labels the smaller generative cell, with its own nucleus represented inside.

00:00:48.616 --> 00:00:52.996
The boundary around E is a cell boundary; the oval at D is a nucleus.

00:00:53.876 --> 00:00:56.953
Counting every circle as a separate cell would therefore give the wrong

00:00:56.953 --> 00:00:57.256
answer.

00:00:57.976 --> 00:01:00.556
This board illustrates a two celled pollen stage.

00:01:01.416 --> 00:01:04.976
Some species shed pollen at this stage, while others shed it after the

00:01:04.976 --> 00:01:06.396
generative cell has already divided.

00:01:06.956 --> 00:01:10.716
The pollen grain is the male gametophyte, not simply one sperm cell.

00:01:11.756 --> 00:01:15.376
Distinguish the whole gametophyte, its cells and the nuclei within those cells

00:01:15.836 --> 00:01:16.716
before applying a count.

00:01:16.872 --> 00:01:19.352
The second board compares selected stages.

00:01:20.232 --> 00:01:23.492
A contains one vegetative nucleus and a generative cell.

00:01:24.172 --> 00:01:28.593
The arrow represents mitosis of the generative cell, producing two haploid

00:01:28.593 --> 00:01:28.832
male

00:01:28.832 --> 00:01:29.132
gametes.

00:01:29.832 --> 00:01:33.413
This is not the earlier meiosis of a diploid microspore mother cell in the

00:01:33.413 --> 00:01:33.752
anther.

00:01:34.772 --> 00:01:37.352
B shows a germinating example after that division.

00:01:38.052 --> 00:01:41.956
The small circles in its tube represent the male gametes, while the oval is

00:01:41.956 --> 00:01:42.112
the

00:01:42.112 --> 00:01:42.972
vegetative nucleus.

00:01:43.552 --> 00:01:47.132
Their relative positions are illustrative rather than a universal migration

00:01:47.132 --> 00:01:47.432
order.

00:01:48.392 --> 00:01:52.229
If pollen is shed at the three celled stage, the two male gametes already

00:01:52.229 --> 00:01:52.492
exist

00:01:52.492 --> 00:01:53.392
before germination.

00:01:54.132 --> 00:01:57.292
Do not make one developmental timetable a rule for every species.

00:01:57.888 --> 00:02:01.448
At B, the pollen tube emerges through a gap in exine.

00:02:02.228 --> 00:02:06.028
It is an outgrowth of the vegetative cell and provides a route for delivery of

00:02:06.028 --> 00:02:06.928
the male gametes.

00:02:07.608 --> 00:02:11.608
On a receptive stigma, successful growth depends on the pollen pistil

00:02:11.608 --> 00:02:15.008
interaction, not merely on a grain landing anywhere.

00:02:15.908 --> 00:02:20.068
Pollination is the transfer of pollen to the stigma; fertilisation is a later

00:02:20.068 --> 00:02:20.768
fusion event.

00:02:21.688 --> 00:02:25.588
Pollen can also germinate in suitable laboratory medium, but laboratory

00:02:25.588 --> 00:02:29.588
germination alone does not prove that a particular pistil will accept it.

00:02:30.208 --> 00:02:34.468
The drawing does not provide a culture recipe, growth rate measurement or

00:02:34.468 --> 00:02:36.388
evidence that every tube reaches an ovule.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:38.820
The pistil section locates the pathway.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:45.500
A labels the stigma, B the style, C the ovary and D a selected ovule.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:50.362
Follow the paired path from a pollen grain on the stigma, through the style

00:02:50.362 --> 00:02:50.520
and

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:51.240
into the ovary.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:56.040
The path represents one compatible pollen tube, not a claim that a pistil

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.060
accepts only one grain or grows only one tube.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:03.560
The tube does not become the style, and it is not a xylem vessel carrying

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:03.940
water.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:06.760
Different tissues guide and support its growth.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:11.940
The diagram omits other ovules and many cellular details so that the route

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.160
remains easy to trace.

00:03:13.464 --> 00:03:17.584
At the bottom of the selected ovule, the path bends toward the micropylar

00:03:17.584 --> 00:03:17.984
opening.

00:03:18.744 --> 00:03:22.444
In the common route illustrated here, the pollen tube enters through the

00:03:22.444 --> 00:03:24.784
micropyle and then reaches a synergid.

00:03:25.484 --> 00:03:29.124
Do not confuse the micropyle with the hilum, which is the attachment junction

00:03:29.124 --> 00:03:30.924
discussed in the previous class.

00:03:31.804 --> 00:03:35.384
Nor should the tube be drawn through the egg before it reaches the embryo sac.

00:03:36.124 --> 00:03:40.304
Other routes of ovule entry occur in some plants, so the selected common

00:03:40.304 --> 00:03:42.264
pathway is not a universal claim.

00:03:43.164 --> 00:03:46.844
Section orientation can turn this route upside down on a page; structure

00:03:46.844 --> 00:03:49.444
relationships matter more than whether the arrow points down.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:52.620
The final board enlarges the micropylar region.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:57.240
The tube enters the left synergid through the represented filiform apparatus.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:01.060
Two male gametes are shown released into that synergid.

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:05.740
The central egg is separate, and the right synergid is not a second egg.

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:10.373
The filiform apparatus is a specialised wall structure associated with

00:04:10.373 --> 00:04:10.820
synergid

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:12.820
function and pollen tube guidance.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:17.260
It is not a bundle of flagella used by sperm to swim through the style.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:21.700
The drawing omits most of the embryo sac boundary and the integuments.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:26.840
Treat the destination arrows as a conceptual summary rather than a measured

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:28.340
movie of gamete movement.

00:04:28.728 --> 00:04:30.548
Follow the two destination arrows.

00:04:31.228 --> 00:04:35.231
One male gamete fuses with the haploid egg to form the diploid zygote:

00:04:35.231 --> 00:04:35.688
syngamy.

00:04:36.508 --> 00:04:40.648
The other fuses with the central cell nuclear complement, represented here by

00:04:40.648 --> 00:04:45.348
two haploid polar nuclei, producing the triploid primary endosperm nucleus.

00:04:45.928 --> 00:04:47.848
That second event is triple fusion.

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:52.008
The vegetative nucleus is not one of those three participating nuclei.

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:56.688
Syngamy and triple fusion together constitute double fertilisation in the

00:04:56.688 --> 00:04:58.108
typical angiosperm model.

00:04:58.748 --> 00:05:02.508
The embryo develops from the zygote, whereas endosperm develops through the

00:05:02.508 --> 00:05:03.188
other pathway.

00:05:03.808 --> 00:05:07.948
The board summarises these destinations; it does not already depict a mature

00:05:07.948 --> 00:05:11.184
seed or every possible endosperm ploidy.
